> end, she decided to risk those eels, and they really weren't very
> tough, even while wearing -3 boots of levitation.

Boots of levitation don't help against eels drowning you.

There is an easy way of dealing with them: get some rocks from higher up
the dungeon (about 40 will suffice), and wait in the middle of the
little peninsula just outside the starting room (Titan version) or one
step away from the shore of the starting island, and let the eels get
near the shore. Then kill them by hitting them with the rocks. About 4
rocks per eel will do. No danger at all.

Remember that eels are not randomly generated, not even on water levels
like Medusa. Once all are gone, none are randomly generated anymore, so
the level is safe from sea monsters from then on.

